<title>BELGIUM: EU clears North Sea Liner Conference.</title>
<headline>EU clears North Sea Liner Conference.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had cleared the North Sea Liner Conference Agreement in the maritime transport sector.</p>
<p>Under this agreement three shipping lines, Finncarriers, Poseidon and United Baltic Corporation, jointly operate a regular ferry providing cargo transport services between ports and points in Finland, Belgium, the Netherlands, Britain and Ireland.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission has...decided to grant this agreement an individual temporary exemption. Accordingly, the maritime activities are exempted for a period of six years and inland activities are exempted for a period of three years,&quot; the Commission said in a statement. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 Fred Dahl</p>
</text>
